.DS_Store
*.local

# `.env` on its own matches ONLY the file named exactly `.env`. It does not
# match `.env.production`, `.env.local`, `.env.staging` and so on — which is
# exactly how `.env.production` ended up tracked in this repo. `.env*` covers
# every variant, so a future `.env.local` holding a real secret cannot be
# committed by accident.
#
# Caveat: .gitignore only governs UNTRACKED files. `.env.production` is already
# tracked and stays tracked — it holds a public backend URL and serves as the
# build-time fallback if Vercel's dashboard VITE_API_URL is ever missing. To
# genuinely stop tracking it: `git rm --cached .env.production`.
.env*

.vercel

# A nested clone of the backend repo (it has happened) must never be linted,
# committed, or pushed from this repo.
openi-hub-backend/
